details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two rustic ceramic plates centered in the frame, angled at 3/4 overhead to showcase the volume of the dish with generous negative space. The foreground plate is in sharp focus, while the second plate sits slightly behind, softly blurred. The scene is illuminated by soft, natural morning light from a window on the left, casting subtle, gentle shadows. The surface is a textured, aged oak wood tabletop with visible grain. Each plate holds two thick slices of golden-brown, crisp sprouted whole-grain bread, generously spread with a chunky, vibrant green mashed avocado, brightened by fine flecks of lemon zest. Over the avocado sits a layer of fresh, peppery baby arugula and ruby-red halved cherry tomatoes. Large, succulent pieces of silvery-white sardine fillets are arranged atop the vegetables, not stacked, but laid clearly across the toast. A light, rustic sprinkle of crushed red pepper flakes adds tiny specks of color across the fish. Alongside the toast, a small, natural portion of halved fresh strawberries rests directly on the plate. A silver fork lies casually on the wood surface near the plates. Scattered nearby are a few stray baby arugula leaves, a small lemon rind remnant, and a light dusting of red pepper flakes, suggesting a lived-in kitchen environment. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a tiny avocado smudge on the rim, slightly uneven browning on the toast. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
  }
]
